@obverse
1. 2 ME ŠU GUR ŠE.BAR SAG-du ZAG
#tr.en.(o 6): 260 kor barley, the principal of the impost, the sūtu-obligation of Šamaš-īpuš, the ploughman from Tabini-ša-Šumu-ukīn, property of the Lady-of-Uruk and Nanāya, pertaining to the sūtu of Šumu-ukīn, son of Bēl-zēri, descendant of Basia, are the debt of Šamaš-īpuš, son of Ardia. 
2. GIŠ.BAN₂ ša₂ {m}{d}UTU-DU₃-uš {lu₂}ENGAR
3. ša₂ ina {garin}ta-bi-ni# ša₂# {m}MU.GIN NIG₂.GA
4. {d}GAŠAN ša₂ UNUG{ki} u {d}na-na-a ša₂ GIŠ.BAN₂
5. ša₂ {m}MU-GIN A-šu₂ ša₂ {m}EN-NUMUN A {m}ba-si-ia
6. ina muh-hi {m}{d}UTU-DU₃-uš A-šu₂ ša₂ {m}IR₃-a
7. ina {iti}GU₄ ina ma-ši-hu ša₂ {d}GAŠAN ša₂ UNUG{ki}
#tr.en.(o 9): He will deliver (the barley) in Month II using the measure of the Lady-of-Uruk. (This is) apart from the previous debt notes charged against him.
8. i-nam-din e-lat u₂-il₃-ti₃ mah-ri-ti
9. ša₂ ina muh-hi-šu₂
